The [[Northern Conquest of Burawa]] was a period of expansions of the primarily coastal [[Kingdom of Burawa]] into the inland regions of Burawa from 893 to 925. The invasions were stymied by the desire to control the  resources that were traded from the interior of Burawa such as gold, silver and other rare minerals through the Kingdom of Burawa to the Mesogean. The conquest had seen the collapse of the [[Kingdom of Ufyen]], [[Kingdom of Sago]] and the [[Kingdom of Iracwi]] during this time and unification of all lands south of the [[Kaftian Mountain Range]].

== Causes of War ==
The Kingdom of Burawa  had been acting as a middleman for trade between the inland [[Qaysanic Burawa|Qaysanic Kingdoms]] for multiple centuries, and the king, [[Iacob II]] had desired to reduce his reliance on the kingdoms and reduce the power of the merchant class by being the sole controller of the minerals that came from the [[Iracwi Highlands]].